=== 3. INTERPRETATION ===
  ACTUAL type-I error at nominal alpha=0.05: 8% (aaft null, 60 draws)
  Six onsets on a 21-year grid admit only ~10-15 effectively
  independent event configurations, so the permutation p-value is
  granular and its tails are heavy. Nominal p-values from this
  test are therefore optimistic by roughly a factor of two, and
  the comparison below is used instead of them.

  CALIBRATED comparison — T3 AUC under NO signal (delta=0):
    mean 0.4915  sd 0.1077  median 0.4741  95th pct 0.6774  max 0.6911
    candidates at or above the 95th percentile (0.6774): NONE

  MINIMUM DETECTABLE EFFECT at 80% power: delta = 1.0 sd (nominal; ~1.5 sd once the type-I inflation above is allowed for).
  So the test DOES have power against a clean, strong lead
  signal. A step of >= 1.0 sd over the 15 days before
  each onset would have been found. Nothing in the corpus
  produces one. Effects below ~0.5 sd remain genuinely untested.

  best observed: drawdown AUC 0.6735, p_shift = 0.0424, p_aaft = 0.0547 (NOT significant)
  9 candidates were screened, so even a p near 0.05 would still need
  a multiplicity correction before it counted as a finding.

  No advance-warning capability is claimed by this script. It
  measures what the existing evaluation can and cannot establish.
